{% set stages = stages_path %}
# OpenSpec configuration. A starter file of the harness template: created once,
# then owned by the project. The PROJECT, STACK and PACKAGE BOUNDARIES blocks
# are filled in by the project; the rest are shared process rules.
schema: spec-driven

context: |
  LANGUAGE. All artifacts (proposal, specs, design, tasks) are written in
  English. Capability and change names are kebab-case. Domain terms come from
  the spec's terms section and are used exactly in their defined meaning.

  PROJECT. What the system does, for whom, what its main value is — fill in.

  STACK. Languages, key libraries, rules for using them — fill in.

  PACKAGE BOUNDARIES. Package map and dependency graph — fill in. A design
  that breaks this graph is wrong regardless of convenience.

  THREE PLACES OF KNOWLEDGE, do not confuse:
  - "{{ spec_path }} — the spec. Requirements and domain. Owned by the owner."
    The source of truth. Read it, do not add to it. Revision journal — {{ revisions_path }}.
  - "openspec/specs/ — implemented behavior by capability. Derived from the spec."
  - "knowledge/ — accumulated knowledge: decisions and their reasons, lessons, quirks"
    of external APIs, open questions. Neither requirements nor behavior.

  STAGES. Implementation goes strictly by the stages in the spec's stages
  section; stage states are the table {{ stages }}. One stage — several
  changes, a change name starts with the stage number (stage3-<name>). A stage
  is closed when all its changes are archived and its acceptance criterion is
  met. A change from the next stage does not start until the current one is
  closed.

rules:
  proposal:
    - "Every requirement must reference a spec paragraph ({{ spec_path }}), e.g. \"§4\". There must be no requirement that is not in the spec — instead of inventing one, ask the owner and stop the work."
    - "Name the stage the change belongs to and why it comes right now."
    - "Do not propose new metrics, table fields or states that are not in the spec."
    - "An \"Out of scope\" section is required: what this change deliberately does not do."
  specs:
    - "Describe observable behavior, not implementation. Type and function names go in design, not here."
    - "Use spec terms exactly in their meaning."
    - "Name thresholds and zones by the spec parameter name, not by a number."
  design:
    - "List the affected packages and check that the change does not break the dependency graph."
    - "All thresholds, zones and windows come from configuration. There must be no numeric literal in the design."
    - "If a contract from the \"Sources of truth\" table of AGENTS.md changes — say so explicitly and refer to the contract-change skill."
    - "A deviation from the spec is allowed but must be named a deviation with a reason, not quietly built into the design."
  tasks:
    - "TDD order: first the \"write a failing test\" step, then \"implement\". Not the other way round."
    - "One step — one meaningful commit. A half-day step is not a step."
{% if rust and monorepo %}
    - "The last step is always the full checks: cargo fmt --all --check, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings, cargo test --workspace{% if frontend %}, bun run typecheck, bun run lint, bun run test, bun run build{% endif %}."
{% elif rust %}
    - "The last step is always the full checks: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings, cargo test."
{% else %}
    - "The last step is always the full checks: bun run typecheck, bun run lint, bun run test, bun run build."
{% endif %}

operations:
  apply:
    guidance:
      - "Work by TDD: test before implementation, red before green."
      - "Do not mark a task done until the corresponding check has actually run and passed."
      - "A bug on the way — do not fix it by guesswork: systematic-debugging first, then the fix."
  archive:
    guidance:
      - "Before archiving, run the subagents spec-auditor{% if rust %}, rust-reviewer{% endif %}{% if frontend %}, frontend-reviewer{% endif %} and attach their output to the summary."
      - "In the summary, state: what deviated from the spec and why, what could not be verified without live data."
      - "Decisions that have a reason move to {{ decisions_path }}; open questions — to {{ open_questions_path }}."
